Tue Nov 10 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Kevin Deldycke <kevin@deldycke.com>

- Update to 8.3.0.
- Drop the boltons and xmltodict requirements: 8.3.0 no longer
  uses them.
- Drop the packageurl-python requirement: only mpm sbom uses it
  now, and openSUSE ships neither of the other two libraries it
  needs.
- Raise the click-extra floor to 10, and the extra-platforms floor
  to 14, which click-extra 10 requires.
- Drop the tomlkit test requirement: the documentation tests now
  use tomlrt, and skip themselves without it.
- Add pytest-xdist to the test requirements: the suite sets its
  xdist_group marker and rejects a marker no plugin registers.
- Stop deselecting test_extra_labels_in_pyproject: it now skips
  itself outside a git checkout.
- Drop the platformdirs suggestion: 8.3.0 no longer uses it.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Oct 31 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Kevin Deldycke <kevin@deldycke.com>

- Update to 8.2.0.
- Raise the packageurl-python floor to 0.17.6: below it, parsing a
  pURL spec raises TypeError.
- Skip test_extra_labels_in_pyproject in %check: it fails on any
  newer extra-platforms that adds a platform to a group, like 13.13.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Oct 22 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Kevin Deldycke <kevin@deldycke.com>

- Update to 8.1.2.
- Raise the click-extra floor to 9.3 and the extra-platforms floor
  to 13.10.
- Run the 8.1.2 test suite, which reads the documentation files it
  checks from the unpacked source rather than from the installed
  module, so %check passes under %pytest again.

